<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bohemian–Hungarian War (1468–1478)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1468–1478</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Bohemian–Hungarian War of 1468–1478 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/matthias-corvinus">Matthias Corvinus</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-of-podebrady">George of Poděbrady</a>, the Hussite king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, and then his successor Vladislaus II Jagiellon. Matthias, presenting himself as a champion of the Catholic Church, conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, Silesia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lusatia">Lusatia</a>; the peace settlement of 1478–1479 left him those lands while Vladislaus kept Bohemia proper.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohemian-hungarian-war-1468-1478.jpg" alt="Bohemian–Hungarian War (1468–1478)" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolf Liebscher · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Adolf_Liebscher_-_Ji%C5%99%C3%AD_z_Pod%C4%9Bbrad_nad_obkl%C3%AD%C4%8Den%C3%BDmi_vojsky.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
